# NSG — PHY/MAC on the mmWave DATA PATH. Chosen over ICIC, and why that matters.
#
# ── The batch this REPLACED, and the check that killed it ──────────────────
# `tools/param_audit.py` ranked LteFfr*/LteFr* (frequency reuse / ICIC) as the
# largest backlog block: ~56 attributes, a real 3GPP feature, completely
# unexposed. It was the obvious next batch. Reading mmwave-helper.cc first:
#   * inside InstallSingleEnbDevice (the mmWave gNB installer) the FFR algorithm
#     creation is COMMENTED OUT, with the fork author's note that using it
#     required changing the bandwidth to 25;
#   * the FFR SAP wiring is commented out and labelled `/* not used in mmwave */`;
#   * FFR is live only in InstallSingleLteEnbDevice — the single LTE anchor.
# In this scenario the anchor carries no user data (every UE is dual-connected
# and all traffic rides the mmWave gNBs), so ICIC would have been an inter-cell
# interference feature with one cell and nothing to coordinate. Twenty minutes
# of source reading against a multi-day dead end.
#
# It also exposed a LIMIT OF THE AUDIT TOOL worth remembering: param_audit
# measures whether a field changes the ENGINE PAYLOAD, not whether it changes
# PHYSICS. Every FFR field would have shown up as WIRED while doing nothing.
# Payload delivery is necessary, not sufficient — that is what these tests are.
#
# ── WIRED (all plain ns-3 attributes; no C++ in this batch) ────────────────
# Deliberately the MmWave* classes, not their Lte* namesakes, for the same
# reason ICIC died: Lte*Phy knobs only touch the idle anchor.
#   ue_noise_figure_db / gnb_noise_figure_db -> MmWaveUePhy/EnbPhy::NoiseFigure
#   ue_tx_power_dbm                          -> MmWaveUePhy::TxPower  (uplink budget)
#   ue_outage_threshold_db, ue_n310          -> UE-side link failure detection
#   cqi_report_period_ms, cqi_timer_threshold_ms -> feedback freshness/ageing
#   sinr_estimate_period_us,
#   ue_sinr_estimate_period_us               -> MmWaveEnbPhy::Update*SinrEstimatePeriod.
#       This is the INPUT the Phase-2b handover loop reads: a mobility decision
#       can only be as fresh as the SINR estimate behind it, so it pairs with
#       ho_check_period_ms.
#   fixed_mcs_dl / fixed_mcs_ul              -> FixedMcs* + McsDefault* (two
#       attributes each: the flag and the value). Removes AMC from an experiment.
#   sched_direction                          -> DlSchedOnly / UlSchedOnly
#   sym_per_slot, ra_preambles,
#   ra_preamble_trans_max, ra_response_window
# numberOfRaPreambles rides the scenario GlobalValue, not the attribute — the
# scenario Config::SetDefault's that one AFTER cmd.Parse and would overwrite it
# (the same trap HARQ hit in radio-2c.patch).
#
# ── NOT SHIPPED: the data error model crashes when disabled ────────────────
# MmWaveSpectrumPhy::DataErrorModelEnabled=false null-dereferences at
# t=0.101 s ("Attempted to dereference zero pointer", ptr.h:718) — something
# downstream dereferences the error model unconditionally. No schema field, same
# rule as the dead schedulers in radio-2c.patch: a config must not be able to
# produce a crashed run. NSG_DATA_ERR still reaches the engine API for research,
# and test_phy_mac.py asserts the BROKEN state so an upstream fix surfaces.
#
# ── sched_direction is the honest answer to "TDD frame format" ─────────────
# radio-2c.patch recorded the frame-format field as N/A because this MAC is
# flexible-TTI: the DL/UL symbol split comes from demand every slot, so there is
# no DDDSU pattern to configure. DlSchedOnly/UlSchedOnly is the real DL/UL
# control it does offer, and it is absolute: measured UL 8324 -> 0 kbps.
#
# ── Measured (2026-07-26, engines/nsoran/test_phy_mac.py, PASS) ────────────
# 3 cells, 6 UEs, 50 Mbps/UE offered, shadowing on:
#
#   A  defaults                     17.82 Mbps/UE  PRB 29.5  UL 8324 kbps
#   B  UE noise figure 5 -> 13 dB   17.56          PRB 38.3  UL 8164
#   C  DL MCS pinned to 4            2.47          PRB 52.5
#   D  DL MCS pinned to 20          16.52          PRB 27.7
#   F  scheduler DL-only            17.91          PRB 29.5  UL 0
#   G  CQI/SINR/RACH/sym batch      18.35          PRB 32.3  UL 8279
#
# * MCS pinning: 2.47 -> 16.52 Mbps/UE (+568%) between MCS 4 and MCS 20. The
#   sharpest lever in the batch, and the one that lets an experiment hold link
#   adaptation still.
# * DL-only: uplink goes to exactly 0.
# * NOISE FIGURE — MEASURE THE RIGHT COLUMN. A worse receiver moved throughput
#   by only -1.5%, which reads as "no effect", while PRB rose 29.5 -> 38.3
#   (+30%). The UEs are offered more than the link delivers, so a degraded link
#   is answered by spending MORE RESOURCES for the same delivered bits. The cost
#   is real; it just lands in PRB, not throughput. Asserting on throughput would
#   have declared a working lever dead — the same class of mistake as measuring
#   a demand-limited run in antenna-2c.patch.
